SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"People's Republic of China: 2021 Article IV Consultation-Press Release; Staff Report; and Statement by the Executive Director for the People's Republic of China","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-01-28","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/cr/issues/2022/01/26/peoples-republic-of-china-2021-article-iv-consultation-press-release-staff-report-and-512248","claim":"China's recovery was advanced but unbalanced; momentum slowed because of rapid withdrawal of fiscal support, lagging consumption amid recurrent COVID-19 outbreaks, slowing real estate investment, and tech-sector regulatory measures that increased policy uncertainty.","locator":"Summary, lines 233-235","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"IMF staff report summarizing contemporaneous macro conditions and policy effects with explicit diagnostic language.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly informs the 2022 policy environment and inherited conditions Xi faced in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attribution is indirect but relevant: these were national policy settings and constraints under Xi's rule, not a claim of personal technocratic skill.","contrary_evidence":["This is an IMF assessment, not a finding that Xi personally designed every measure or outcome."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.4","5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Rebalancing Act: China's 2022 Outlook","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-01-12","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/opinion/2022/01/12/rebalancing-act-china-s-2022-outlook","claim":"The World Bank said China entered 2022 with slower growth, downside risks from renewed COVID outbreaks and prolonged real-estate weakness, and needed a greater role for markets and the private sector rather than investment-led stimulus.","locator":"Opinion text, middle paragraphs on the 2022 outlook","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"World Bank commentary based on current macro analysis, but it is an opinion piece rather than a formal country report.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the 2022 target year at its start.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant to Xi because it describes the policy direction and constraints of the national economy under his leadership.","contrary_evidence":["It is advisory and not proof that Xi accepted or implemented the recommended course."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.4","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Economic Restructuring Key to Coping with Risks in China's Economy","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-06-16","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/opinion/2022/06/16/economic-restructuring-key-to-coping-with-risks-in-china-s-economy","claim":"The World Bank said recurrent COVID outbreaks and lockdowns disrupted supply chains and household/business activity, the 2022 growth outlook had been cut to 4.3 percent, and policy should shift toward consumption, labor mobility, and structural rebalancing.","locator":"Opinion text, paragraphs describing the 2022 outlook and policy advice","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Strong macro analysis, but still an opinion-oriented World Bank piece rather than a formal finding of intent or implementation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the middle of 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant: it evaluates the national policy mix under Xi's rule and the policy response available to the leadership.","contrary_evidence":["The article recommends reforms; it does not show Xi personally embraced them."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.4","5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Chinese property developers face big debt maturities in 2022","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-01-19","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/chinese-property-developers-face-big-debt-maturities-in-2022-2742100","claim":"Chinese property developers faced $117 billion of debt maturing in 2022 and an unprecedented liquidity squeeze after Beijing's campaign to rein in borrowing in the sector.","locator":"Lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting with concrete sector metrics and direct policy context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and describes the inherited property-sector problem Xi had to manage.","ruler_attribution":"Attribution is indirect but relevant because the tightening campaign and its consequences arose under Xi's national policy setting.","contrary_evidence":["This does not by itself show whether the crackdown was prudent or reckless."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.4","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China vows timely home deliveries in wake of property protests","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-07-14","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/china-vows-timely-home-deliveries-in-wake-of-property-protests-2847129","claim":"Chinese regulators stepped in to help local governments guarantee delivery of unfinished homes after mortgage-payment boycotts spread, reflecting a targeted rescue response to property-sector unrest.","locator":"Lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reported a contemporaneous, policy-specific intervention with clear sectoral consequences.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to Xi because the intervention was part of the national policy response under his leadership, though the immediate action came through regulators.","contrary_evidence":["The rescue response mitigated harm but also confirms the severity of the underlying property stress."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Analysis: China's mortgage boycott spurs shakeout among strapped developers","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-07-20","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/analysis-chinas-mortgage-boycott-spurs-shakeout-among-strapped-developers-2849149","claim":"Reuters described a revolt by homebuyers over unfinished projects as forcing a shakeout among cash-starved developers who had relied on apartment pre-sales.","locator":"Lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters analysis based on contemporaneous market developments and a specific mechanism of distress.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant because the phenomenon reflected the policy and regulatory environment under Xi's rule.","contrary_evidence":["This is an analysis piece, not a government finding or formal audit."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Chinese developers in 'survival mode' slash property investment","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-08-14","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/chinas-janjuly-property-investment-falls-at-fastest-pace-since-march-2020-2871966","claim":"Reuters said Chinese developers sharply cut property investment in July 2022 and new construction starts suffered their biggest fall in nearly a decade.","locator":"Lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting using official and market data on a major growth sector.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to Xi because the property downturn unfolded under his national policy regime and affected the macro trajectory he controlled.","contrary_evidence":["The article reports sector stress; it does not prove Xi's policy choices were the sole cause."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.4","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Factbox-China's 20th Communist Party Congress: who could be in Xi's new team?","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-10-12","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/factboxchinas-20th-communist-party-congress-who-could-be-in-xis-new-team-2911027","claim":"Reuters identified Li Qiang as a close Xi ally and He Lifeng as a longtime ally who headed the state planning commission, while reformers such as Hu Chunhua were expected to step down.","locator":"Factbox entries for Li Qiang, He Lifeng, and Hu Chunhua","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters factbox on imminent elite appointments with direct relevance to economic policymaking personnel.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to Xi because these were the personnel choices surrounding his consolidation of economic authority.","contrary_evidence":["Expected promotions are not the same as proven economic competence."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China's Xi clinches third term, packs leadership with loyalists","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-10-23","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/chinas-xi-clinches-third-term-packs-leadership-with-loyalists-2919033","claim":"Xi secured a precedent-breaking third term and introduced a top governing body stacked with loyalists, cementing his power over the party.","locator":"Lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters contemporaneous report on the outcome of the Party Congress.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Xi as the beneficiary and center of the leadership reshuffle.","contrary_evidence":["This is a political power fact, not itself an economic performance measure."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Full text of resolution on Party Constitution amendment","publisher":"gov.cn / Xinhua","publication_date":"2022-10-22","url":"https://english.www.gov.cn/news/topnews/202210/22/content_WS6353e0bbc6d0a757729e18c7.html","claim":"The Party Constitution was amended to add common prosperity, a domestic-economy-centered development pattern, and language calling for higher-quality, more equitable, sustainable, and secure economic development.","locator":"Paragraphs 63-65","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official Party Congress text showing declared economic priorities and Xi-centered ideological direction.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant because this was Xi's congress and the amended constitution reflects his leadership agenda.","contrary_evidence":["Declared goals are not the same as implemented outcomes."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"National Economy Withstood Pressure and Reached a New Level in 2022","publisher":"National Bureau of Statistics of China","publication_date":"2023-01-17","url":"https://www.stats.gov.cn/english/PressRelease/202301/t20230117_1892094.html?appsule=61","claim":"China's GDP grew 3.0 percent in 2022; the economy faced a midyear downturn, then recovery after a package of stabilization policies, with employment and prices described as generally stable.","locator":"Section 1 and Section 2","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official statistical communiqué with the headline macro result and the government's own explanation of the policy response.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the full target year.","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to Xi because this is the national economic outcome under his rule, though not a personalized performance audit.","contrary_evidence":["Official statistics may reflect government framing and do not isolate Xi's personal contribution."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Households' Income and Consumption Expenditure in 2022","publisher":"National Bureau of Statistics of China","publication_date":"2023-01-18","url":"https://www.stats.gov.cn/english/PressRelease/202301/t20230118_1892303.html","claim":"Nationwide real disposable income rose 2.9 percent in 2022; rural residents' real income rose faster than urban residents'; and real household consumption fell 0.2 percent.","locator":"Section I and Section II","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official household-income dataset with urban-rural breakdowns and real terms.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to Xi because it shows household welfare outcomes under his rule, though not a direct causal estimate of his policy alone.","contrary_evidence":["Average income gains coexisted with weak consumption and a large urban-rural gap."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.8","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Investment in Fixed Assets from January to December 2022","publisher":"National Bureau of Statistics of China","publication_date":"2023-01-18","url":"https://www.stats.gov.cn/english/PressRelease/202301/t20230118_1892297.html","claim":"Fixed-asset investment rose 5.1 percent in 2022, with infrastructure up 9.4 percent, manufacturing up 9.1 percent, high-tech manufacturing and services reported as strong, health and social work up 26.1 percent, private investment up only 0.9 percent, and property development down 10.0 percent.","locator":"Main table and opening paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official investment dataset with sectoral detail directly relevant to policy mix and trajectory.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to Xi because the investment mix reflects the national economic strategy and constraints under his leadership.","contrary_evidence":["Strong state-led and high-tech investment coexisted with very weak private investment and a property slump."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.4","5B.6","5B.8","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"National Real Estate Development and Sales in 2022","publisher":"National Bureau of Statistics of China","publication_date":"2023-01-18","url":"https://www.stats.gov.cn/english/PressRelease/202301/t20230118_1892298.html","claim":"Real estate development investment fell 10.0 percent in 2022; housing starts fell 39.4 percent; sales area fell 24.3 percent; and funding for developers fell 25.9 percent.","locator":"Opening paragraphs and investment table","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official sector statistics with direct relevance to the property crisis.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to Xi because the property downturn was a central macroeconomic problem under his rule and policy setting.","contrary_evidence":["The report measures the downturn; it does not itself assign blame or assess the policy mix's necessity."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.4","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China's fixed-asset investment maintains stable growth in 2022","publisher":"gov.cn / Xinhua","publication_date":"2023-01-17","url":"https://english.www.gov.cn/archive/statistics/202301/17/content_WS63c61c6fc6d0a757729e5927.html","claim":"The NBS said high-tech manufacturing investment rose 22.2 percent, high-tech services 12.1 percent, infrastructure 9.4 percent, health and social work 26.1 percent, and property development investment fell 10 percent in 2022.","locator":"Body text, paragraphs on sectoral investment","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government summary of the annual investment composition and policy support measures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to Xi because it shows what the state prioritized during his 2022 rule.","contrary_evidence":["The same source shows property weakness and only marginal private-investment growth."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.8","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China's job market remains stable in 2022","publisher":"gov.cn / Xinhua","publication_date":"2023-01-17","url":"https://english.www.gov.cn/archive/statistics/202301/17/content_WS63c61e87c6d0a757729e592e.html","claim":"China created 12.06 million new urban jobs in 2022, but the 16-24 unemployment rate reached 16.7 percent in December and NBS said young people faced greater hiring difficulty.","locator":"Body paragraphs on employment and youth unemployment","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official labor-market release with specific employment outcomes and age-group breakdown.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to Xi because employment outcomes and youth distress were national policy issues under his rule.","contrary_evidence":["Total job creation was strong even though youth unemployment remained elevated."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022年第四季度中国货币政策执行报告","publisher":"People's Bank of China","publication_date":"2023-02-24","url":"https://www.pbc.gov.cn/zhengcehuobisi/125207/125227/125957/4584071/d7e45aa7d98c4664a9a6c2393d16787d/index.html","claim":"The PBC said it cut reserve requirements twice, released more than 1 trillion yuan of long-term funds, used multiple liquidity tools, cut benchmark lending rates, expanded policy-bank credit, and supported property-sector rescue measures in 2022.","locator":"Paragraphs 18-19 in the report summary","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Central-bank report stating the year's policy actions and monetary conditions in detail.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the 2022 policy response, published immediately after year-end.","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to Xi because the report describes the macroeconomic stabilization toolkit deployed under the Party-state leadership he headed.","contrary_evidence":["The report is self-assessment from the central bank and not an independent audit of effectiveness."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.6","5B.9","5B.10"]}

Search and rejection summary
I reviewed roughly 30 distinct documents across IMF, World Bank, Reuters, the NBS, the PBOC, and CPC/NBS official releases. I kept 14 distinct URLs as the best non-duplicative evidence.

Kept because they added distinct value:
- IMF 2022 Article IV on policy uncertainty, slowdown, and rebalancing.
- Two World Bank 2022 outlook/rebalancing pieces on growth slowdown and structural reform needs.
- Reuters on 2022 property debt maturities, mortgage boycott, property-investment collapse, and elite economic appointments.
- Official CPC Congress text on common prosperity and high-quality development.
- NBS annual GDP, household income/consumption, fixed investment, real estate, and jobs releases.
- PBC quarterly monetary-policy report on reserve cuts, liquidity, rates, and property support.

Rejected or deprioritized:
- Duplicate Reuters syndications and mirrored republishes of the same property and congress stories.
- Later 2023-2026 macro commentary that was outside the 2022 target period.
- Generic source pages without period-specific claims.
- Broad World Bank regulatory-efficiency pages and unrelated older history pieces.
- Repetitive official releases that restated the same GDP or employment statistics without adding a materially distinct claim.
- Search results that only repeated the headline without a usable claim locator.

Remaining gaps
- Direct evidence of Xi's personal micro-level economic judgment remains limited; much of the record is attributable to the Party-state and central bank rather than a personally signed Xi directive.
- Distributional evidence is decent for income and urban-rural gaps, but wealth inequality and household balance-sheet stress are still underdeveloped here.
- I have strong evidence on macro stabilization, property stress, and employment, but less direct evidence on whether appointments were chosen for competence versus loyalty beyond the 20th Congress reshuffle.
- More search would help if you want a finer treatment of private-sector policy, local-government debt, or official correction of policy mistakes, but this dossier is already adequate for chapter-level judging.
